---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'
import { teamMembers, teamRegistryAuthority } from '../data/team'
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Research team | Marici"
  description="Canonical Marici research identities, responsibilities, programme interfaces, and epistemic-graph records."
>
  <section class="section-shell" aria-labelledby="team-title">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Research identities</p>
        <h1 id="team-title">One programme, distinct responsibilities.</h1>
      </div>
      <p>
        Marici uses qualified research identities so that claims retain an accountable owner while
        cross-sector work remains part of one shared programme. Roles state responsibility and
        interface; they do not make one researcher’s results authoritative in another’s domain.
      </p>
    </header>

    <aside class="registry-note" aria-label="Registry authority">
      <p><strong>Registry authority</strong></p>
      <p>
        Human policy: <code>{teamRegistryAuthority.humanPolicy}</code>. Durable identities:
        <code>{teamRegistryAuthority.graphSurface}</code> entities of kind
        <code>{teamRegistryAuthority.graphKind}</code>. Programme pages refine roles but do not
        silently replace the canonical identity registry.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <ul class="team-grid" aria-label="Marici team members">
      {teamMembers.map((member) => (
        <li class="team-card">
          <header>
            <div>
              <p class="team-role">{member.role}</p>
              <h2>{member.identity}</h2>
            </div>
            <a href={`/graph/?entity=${encodeURIComponent(member.graphId)}`}>Graph record</a>
          </header>
          <p>{member.contribution}</p>
          <dl>
            <div>
              <dt>Team interface</dt>
              <dd>{member.interface}</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Workspace</dt>
              <dd><code>{member.workspace}</code></dd>
            </div>
            {member.programme && (
              <div>
                <dt>Programme locator</dt>
                <dd><code>{member.programme}</code></dd>
              </div>
            )}
          </dl>
          {member.personaBoundary && <p class="persona-boundary">{member.personaBoundary}</p>}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <article class="role-boundary">
      <p class="eyebrow">Interpretation boundary</p>
      <h2>Roles organize inquiry; they do not certify conclusions.</h2>
      <p>
        Ledger entries and admitted graph records preserve authorship and argumentative provenance.
        Mathematical or physical authority still comes from the stated source, exact verification,
        review boundary, and—where applicable—an independently established Carrier operation.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .registry-note,
  .role-boundary {
    margin-block: 28px;
    padding: 22px 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: rgb(9 22 28 / 72%);
  }

  .registry-note p { margin: 0; }
  .registry-note p + p { margin-top: 8px; color: var(--muted); }

  .team-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .team-card {
    padding: 25px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: linear-gradient(150deg, rgb(15 32 39 / 88%), rgb(9 22 28 / 90%));
  }

  .team-card header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .team-card h2 { margin: 3px 0 0; }
  .team-card > p { color: var(--muted); }
  .team-role { margin: 0; color: var(--accent); font: 650 .7rem Consolas, monospace; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .team-card header a { white-space: nowrap; font-size: .84rem; }

  .team-card dl { margin: 22px 0 0; }
  .team-card dl div + div { margin-top: 14px; }
  .team-card dt { color: var(--dim); font: 650 .68rem Consolas, monospace; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .07em; }
  .team-card dd { margin: 4px 0 0; color: var(--muted); }
  .persona-boundary { padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft); font-size: .9rem; }
  .role-boundary h2 { margin-block: 8px; }

  @media (max-width: 860px) { .team-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .team-card header { flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; } }
</style>
